OL,2,V55555555CFERRY DELAYS EASE
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CAS FRENCH STRIKE ENDS
OL,5, The Easter Dover ferry chaos which left
OL,6, thousands of holidaymakers stranded has
OL,7, eased with the last of the cars held up
OL,8, managing to get away.
OL,10, French Sealink seamen at Calais,
OL,11, Dunkirk and Dieppe voted to end their
OL,12, strike immediately after peace talks.
OL,14, But coaches and lorries at Dover still
OL,15, faced long backlog delays for services
OL,16, hit by the French dispute and the two
OL,17, two month strike by P&O ferry workers.
OL,19, People are still being told "Don't come
OL,20, unless you have a booking" after peace
OL,21, talks to end the P&O dispute failed.
OL,23,F]DFrom 02-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
