OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G8/16
OL,2,V55555555CKINNOCK IN LEADERSHIP
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CBALLOT CALL
OL,5, Labour leader Neil Kinnock has acted
OL,6, swiftly in a bid to ensure that as many
OL,7, Party members as possible can take part
OL,8, in the leadership elections.
OL,10, He suggested the National Executive
OL,11, should lay down guidelines for
OL,12, constituency ballots of individual
OL,13, members when it meets on April 27.
OL,15, Party rules do not demand that every
OL,16, member be balloted.
OL,18, Mr Kinnock, who made the call in a
OL,19, letter to Labour general secretary
OL,20, Larry Whitty, faces a challenge from
OL,21, former Cabinet minister Tony Benn.
OL,23,F]DFrom 02-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
