OL,1,Q{$~k4~{4k7  {$~{4~+$1 ########G10/16
OL,2,Q/.!+.!/*%*%  /*%/*%+.!/$C PUTNEY TO  Qj
OL,3,Q5GBeefeater Gin Trophy  C MORTLAKE   Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FFavourites Oxford cruised to a comfort-
OL,6,Fable victory - their 12th in 13 years -
OL,7,Fin perfect conditions in the 134th race
OL,8,Frace from Putney to Mortlake.
OL,10,FThe only time that Cambridge were ahead
OL,11,Fwas off the start, where Oxford had
OL,12,Fchosen the Surrey station.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThen one Cambridge oar missed a stroke
OL,15,Fand their boat seemed almost to stall.
OL,16,FBy the mile post Oxford, seven seconds
OL,17,Foutside the record, were a length up.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe dark blues quickly added another
OL,20,Ftwo lengths clear water, and from then
OL,21,Fon pulled away to cross the line over
OL,22,Ffive lengths up in a fast 17mins 35secs
OL,23,Q]GFrom 02-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
